Description: Provides auditable multi-trait selection-index tools for plant
    breeding programs. The desired-gain selection index (DGSI) searches for
    coefficients whose realised response approaches breeder-defined targets,
    following Joukhadar et al. (2024) <doi:10.3389/fpls.2024.1337388>.
    The quadratic genomic selection index (QGSI) scores genomic estimated
    breeding values with an explicit linear-weight vector and a validated
    symmetric matrix of squared and cross-product weights, following
    Ceron-Rojas et al. (2026) <doi:10.1038/s41467-026-69890-3>. Results include
    covariance provenance, automatic replicate selection, convergence and
    stability diagnostics, eligibility decisions, rankings, and component-wise
    score contributions.
